{"v":1,"lessons":[{"id":"ja:c1","title":"Notions de grammaire","level":"Débutant","kind":"grammar","intro":"Japanese sentence structure is very similar to that of Korean, so speakers of Korean will find many aspects of Japanese grammar familiar, and vice versa.","sections":[{"heading":"Point 1","body":"Unlike English, which uses the subject-verb-object syntax, Japanese syntax is subject-object-verb. Japanese uses postpositions instead of prepositions (Japan in and not in Japan). However, unlike many European languages, it has no gender, declensions or plurals. Nouns never decline while adjectives follow a generally standard conjugation pattern. However, verbs have extensive conjugation patterns and many Japanese lessons for foreign language learners are about getting these conjugations right. Verbs and adjectives also conjugate by politeness level, though, and in a rather peculiar way."},{"heading":"Point 2","body":"Japanese is an agglutinative language, meaning several morphemes which have purely grammatical functions are glued to the end of a word stem to express the grammatical function. The more the intended meaning differs from the basic form of the word, the more morphemes are glued together."}],"phrases":[],"quiz":[]},{"id":"ja:c2","title":"Premiers mots","level":"Débutant","intro":"Les phrases utiles pour ce thème : premiers mots.","sections":[],"phrases":[{"t":"こんにちは","f":"Bonjour.","r":"Konnichiwa."},{"t":"お元気ですか。","f":"Comment allez-vous ?","r":"O-genki desu ka?"},{"t":"おかげさまで","f":"Très bien, merci.","r":"O-kage-sama de."},{"t":"お名前はなんですか。","f":"Quel est votre nom ?","r":"O-namae ha nan desu ka?"},{"t":"______ と申します。","f":"Mon nom est ______.","r":"____to moshimasu. / ou 私の名前は　____　です。Watashi no namae wa ___"},{"t":"初めまして","f":"Heureux de vous rencontrer.","r":"Hajimemashite."},{"t":"お願いします。","f":"S.v.p.","r":"O-negai shimasu."},{"t":"ありがとう","f":"Merci.","r":"Arigato. / どうも　Do~mo est aussi possible, mais dans un regist"},{"t":"いいえ","f":"Il n'y a pas de quoi","r":"Iie est le même mot que \"non\". C'est la forme modeste. (comm"},{"t":"はい","f":"Oui","r":"Hai"},{"t":"すみません","f":"Pardon","r":"Sumimasen."},{"t":"ごめんなさい","f":"Je suis désolé.","r":"Gomen'nasai."},{"t":"さようなら","f":"Au revoir","r":"Sayounara."},{"t":"すみません ______ を探しています","f":"Excusez-moi, je cherche ______ (pour demander son chemin)","r":"。"},{"t":"日本語を話せません","f":"Je ne parle pas Japonais.","r":"Nihongo wo hanasemasen."},{"t":"フランス語を話しますか。","f":"Parlez-vous français ?","r":"Furansugo wo hanashimasu ka?"},{"t":"ここに誰かフランス語を話せる人はいますか。","f":"Y a-t-il quelqu'un qui parle français ici ?","r":"Koko ni dareka furansugo wo hanaseru hito ha imasu ka?"},{"t":"助けて !","f":"À l'aide !","r":"Tasukete!"},{"t":"お早うございます。","f":"Bonjour (le matin)","r":"O-hayo Gozaimasu"},{"t":"こんばんは","f":"Bonsoir","r":"kombanwa."},{"t":"おやすみなさい","f":"Bonne nuit","r":"O-yasuminasai."},{"t":"分かりません","f":"Je ne comprend pas","r":"wakarimasen."},{"t":"トイレはどこにありますか。","f":"Où sont les toilettes ?","r":"toire wa doko ni arimasu ka ?"},{"t":"こんにちは。 Konnichiwa.","f":"Bonjour. (l’après-midi)","r":"kon-nee-chee-wah"},{"t":"お元気ですか？ O-genki desu ka?","f":"Comment allez-vous ?","r":"Oh-GEN-kee dess-ka?"},{"t":"はい、元気です。 Hai, genki desu.","f":"Très bien, merci.","r":"Ha-ee, gen-kee dess"},{"t":"お名前は？ O-namae wa?","f":"Comment vous appelez-vous ?","r":"Oh-nah-mah-eh wah?"},{"t":"... です。 ... desu.","f":"Je m’appelle…","r":"... dess."},{"t":"始めまして。どうぞ宜しくお願いします。 Hajimemashite. Dōzo yoroshiku onegaishimasu.","f":"Enchanté.","r":"Hah-jee-meh-mash-teh dohh-zoh yoh-roh-sh-ku oh-neh-gah-ee sh"},{"t":"お願いします。 Onegai shimasu.","f":"S’il vous plaît.","r":"oh-neh-gah-ee shee-mahs"},{"t":"どうぞ。 Dōzo.","f":"S’il vous plaît.","r":"Dohh-zoh"},{"t":"ありがとうございます。 Arigatō gozaimasu.","f":"Merci.","r":"ah-ree-GAH-toh go-ZAh-ee-mahs"},{"t":"ありがとう。 Arigatō.","f":"Merci.","r":"ah-ree-GAH-toh"},{"t":"どうも。 Dōmo.","f":"Merci.","r":"doh-moh"},{"t":"おおきに。 Ōkini","f":"Merci.","r":"ohh-KEE-nee"},{"t":"どういたしまして。 Dō itashimashite.","f":"De 